<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Flour says buys 17,300T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Korea Flour says buys 17,300T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Flour Milling Corp said on Friday it has bought 17,300 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from United Grain Corp.  </p>
<p>A company official said shipment was set for December 10- January 10 from the Pacific Northwest to the South Korea's western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follow:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	     Tonne	Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  6,700	 $184.10</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  2,200	 $187.82</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	   4,200	 $191.11</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring    4,200	 $197.40</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
